# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
# Reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
# Format: [source] [destination] [code]. Sources are path-only: full-URL
# sources and Netlify-style "!" flags are ignored. Static rules match the
# exact path, so each URL needs one line per trailing-slash form.

# The aria-cnn-embedders research writeup was removed on purpose (that work
# is over). Old links land on the research index. The destination keeps its
# trailing slash because Pages answers /research with a 308 to /research/,
# which would add a second hop. The index.html form is listed too: Pages
# used to 308 it to the directory URL, and without a rule it would 404.
/research/aria-cnn-embedders/ /research/ 301
/research/aria-cnn-embedders /research/ 301
/research/aria-cnn-embedders/index.html /research/ 301
